{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>So shall be given to him.</b> Rashi explained: it is not giving an actual wound but monetary compensation. And so the law requires: if the first injurer acted without intent, there is no possibility to inflict a break or an equivalent wound upon him. Furthermore, if the wound is in a dangerous place, he might die. And regarding the eye — if one diminished a third of the light of his fellow's eye, a person cannot do the same to the injurer; or if the injurer of the eye is himself blind, what shall they do to him? Therefore the words of our Sages are true. And if one were to object: if the injurer is poor, what shall they do to him? The answer: Scripture speaks of the majority of the world, and perhaps the poor man will become rich. And we find written: ״לא תקחו כופר לנפש רוצח״ (you shall not take ransom for the life of a murderer), which implies that you are permitted to take ransom for limbs."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:01.703936177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}